# This file is generated, like README.md. Edit it in the source repository — a change made
# here is overwritten on the next release.

# Local session-recording state. Codaph writes full Claude Code transcripts here — tool
# calls, file contents, command output — which on a developer machine means verbatim
# material from private repositories. It is never part of the published plugin, and this
# repository is public, so it must never be committed. Tens of megabytes of it can be sitting
# in a working tree at any time; that is fine, and staying untracked is what keeps it fine.
.codaph/

# Dependencies. The plugin ships its bundles committed (see integrations/claude-code/.gitignore,
# which re-includes hooks/dist and mcp/dist for that reason), but never its node_modules.
node_modules/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log

# Local-only leak rules: names that must not be published in the repository they guard.
.github/leakcheck/rules.local.mjs
